> With it, it will flag any escaped quotes.

Are you sure?  The following gives me no problems:

``` js
/*eslint quotes: [2, "double", "avoid-escape"]*/

var escaped = "a string containing \"escaped\" quotes";
```

Here's the problem:

``` js
if (!isValid && avoidEscape) {
    isValid = isSurroundedBy(rawVal, settings.alternateQuote) && rawVal.indexOf(settings.quote) >= 0;
}
```

The `>=0` is applied to the raw representation, which includes the surrounding quotes.

Sorry, one more question, should this result in an error?

``` js
/*eslint quotes: [2, "single", "avoid-escape"]*/

var escaped = "a string containing escaped \'single\' quotes";
```
